1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,717
Every morning,

2
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:02,050
this American
school bus

3
00:00:02,050 --> 00:00:03,433
has to drive
through Canada…

4
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:05,117
just to stay in
the same state.

5
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:06,417
Point Roberts
is right here.

6
00:00:06,517 --> 00:00:08,383
Blaine High is
right over there.

7
00:00:08,567 --> 00:00:10,367
It’s eleven miles
across the bay.

8
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:11,300
Nice shortcut.

9
00:00:11,433 --> 00:00:12,617
Shame there’s
no bridge.

10
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:13,900
So why does
Washington

11
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:15,250
have a piece
stuck over here?

12
00:00:15,367 --> 00:00:17,583
In 1846, diplomats

13
00:00:17,583 --> 00:00:19,033
drew the forty-ninth
parallel

14
00:00:19,033 --> 00:00:20,383
straight across
the map,

15
00:00:20,383 --> 00:00:21,717
accidentally
snipping off

16
00:00:21,717 --> 00:00:23,200
this tiny
peninsula tip.

17
00:00:23,283 --> 00:00:24,633
Which means the
only road out…

18
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:25,800
leads straight into

19
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:26,917
a foreign country.

20
00:00:26,967 --> 00:00:28,150
So the bus
crosses here,

21
00:00:28,333 --> 00:00:29,433
loops twenty-six
miles

22
00:00:29,433 --> 00:00:30,433
through British
Columbia,

23
00:00:30,433 --> 00:00:31,683
and crosses
back into

24
00:00:31,683 --> 00:00:33,017
the U.S. at Blaine.

25
00:00:33,183 --> 00:00:34,533
Two international
borders.

26
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:35,500
Forty minutes.

27
00:00:35,617 --> 00:00:36,850
And the prize
at the end?

28
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:38,000
Algebra.

29
00:00:38,783 --> 00:00:39,533
After school?

30
00:00:39,617 --> 00:00:40,583
They do the entire

31
00:00:40,583 --> 00:00:42,650
international commute
in reverse.

32
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:44,533
Which means these
kids clear

33
00:00:44,533 --> 00:00:45,617
armed customs

34
00:00:45,617 --> 00:00:47,850
four times every
single day…

35
00:00:48,583 --> 00:00:49,267
on a standard

36
00:00:49,267 --> 00:00:50,283
yellow school bus.
